# The whole audit directory: run artifacts, at any depth. An earlier pattern
# of audit/*.jsonl missed audit/attacks/*.jsonl and would have committed 34
# files from a gate run. AuditLog creates the directory at runtime, so nothing
# needs to be committed to hold the place. A "!audit/.gitkeep" negation was
# tried here and does nothing: git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so the exception can never match. Verified by deleting audit/ and rerunning
# the demo.
audit/
